IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hbc-contracts`
IMPORT `hbc-qa`

-- Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (hbc-qa.l4): every exported question, for every
-- role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own roles, with FALSE (the
-- situation does not hold) and every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. Those cases are generated from
-- the exports' own parameter lists (the first section). For the home owner (the baseline's seat) the answers are also
-- asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. The builder's answers are worked by hand from
-- the text, and mirror cases ask the same facts from both seats. The contracts are the baseline cases' own fixtures,
-- copied here unchanged (the baseline cases file is not imported, so its assertions are not run twice).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked contract` IS A Contract
ASSUME `an unasked cause` IS A `Cause of the variation`
ASSUME `an unasked reason` IS A `Reason for a price rise`
ASSUME `an unasked reason of mine` IS A `Reason for my price rise`
ASSUME `an unasked failure` IS A `Who failed`
ASSUME `an unasked failure as the builder sees it` IS A `Who failed, as the builder sees it`
ASSUME `an unasked restriction` IS AN `Inspection restriction`
ASSUME `an unasked kind of complaint` IS A `Kind of complaint`

`as the owner` MEANS `I am the home owner having home building work done`
`as the builder` MEANS `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner`

