§§ `For the home owner`

-- s 3(1), r 2A: $340 000 is within the range; $7 500 is not over $7 500.
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover my contract as the owner` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover my contract as the owner` `as the owner` `a renovation at 7500` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover my contract as the owner` `as the owner` `a renovation at 7500` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my contract a home building work contract` `a renovation at 7500`)

-- s 4(1): unsigned, not made as required.
#ASSERT `Is my contract made the way the Act requires` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my contract made the way the Act requires` `as the owner` `an unsigned build contract` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my contract made the way the Act requires` `as the owner` `an unsigned build contract` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my contract made as the Act requires` `an unsigned build contract`)

-- s 4(3).
#ASSERT `Must I be given the Notice for the Home Owner before I sign` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I be given the Notice for the Home Owner before I sign` `as the owner` `a renovation at 7500` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I be given the Notice for the Home Owner before I sign` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS `yes if` (`Must I be given the notice before I sign` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`)

-- s 5(3): 10 working days; 0 for a contract the Act does not cover.
#ASSERT `Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy of the contract` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS `working days` 10
#ASSERT `Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy of the contract` `as the owner` `a renovation at 7500` EQUALS `working days` 0
#ASSERT `Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy of the contract` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS `working days` (`Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`)

-- s 10(1)(a): 6.5% of $340 000 is $22 100; r 3A: 20% of $30 000 cabinetry is $6 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most deposit my builder may take before work starts` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS amount 22100
#ASSERT `What is the most deposit my builder may take before work starts` `as the owner` `a cabinetry contract at 30000 with a 20 per cent deposit` EQUALS amount 6000
#ASSERT `What is the most deposit my builder may take before work starts` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS amount (`What is the most deposit my builder may take` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`)

-- s 10(1).
#ASSERT `Do the payment terms of my contract break the limits` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do the payment terms of my contract break the limits` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS `yes if` (`Do my contract's payment terms break the limits` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`)

-- s 10(3), (5): for work done, yes; not for work done and off the schedule, no.
#ASSERT `Once work has started may my builder demand this payment` `as the owner` TRUE `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Once work has started may my builder demand this payment` `as the owner` TRUE `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Once work has started may my builder demand this payment` `as the owner` TRUE `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May my builder demand this progress payment` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 14(1), (2).
#ASSERT `Is my cost plus contract missing the heading or acknowledgment` `as the owner` `a cost plus build at 300000 with no heading` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my cost plus contract missing the heading or acknowledgment` `as the owner` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my cost plus contract missing the heading or acknowledgment` `as the owner` `a cost plus build at 300000 with no heading` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my cost plus contract missing its heading or acknowledgment` `a cost plus build at 300000 with no heading`)

-- ss 4(5), 19(2): unsigned, before completion: yes; after completion: no.
#ASSERT `May I end my contract for the way it was made` `as the owner` `an unsigned build contract` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I end my contract for the way it was made` `as the owner` `an unsigned build contract` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I end my contract for the way it was made` `as the owner` `a cost plus build at 300000 with no heading` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May I terminate my contract for the way it was made` `a cost plus build at 300000 with no heading` FALSE)

-- s 8: a direction with the statement in 5 working days needs no signature; in 12, it does; an agreed change always.
